## Program Outcome

The hosted dashboard provides a controlled, explainable attention queue and a bounded recent-change
feed for daily review. It preserves per-instance freshness, keeps unresolved state independent from
browser visit markers, avoids cadence-generated history, and directs investigation back to safe
local Tool Shed routes without remote control.

## M1-ATTENTION-AND-CHANGE-TRUTH — Implement controlled projections

Status: active
Depends on: none

Outcome: Derive stable attention items and normalized recent events from existing accepted state,
freshness, App Server failure groups, material events, and lifecycle events.

Gates:

- `G1-ATTENTION-CONTRACT`: controlled reason registry; explicit severity, source, first/current
  timestamps, freshness, deterministic deduplication and clearing; no arbitrary reporter text.
- `G2-RECENT-CHANGE-SEMANTICS`: change-only normalized feed; existing retention; browser-local
  last-visit presentation state; unresolved attention remains active regardless of visit state.

Candidate campaign: `implement-actionable-dashboard-attention-and-recent-changes`.

## M2-ACTIONABLE-DASHBOARD-WORK2 — Render and qualify the daily-review experience

Status: active
Depends on: M1

Outcome: Present fleet/project attention details and recent changes with stable links, source and
freshness context, accessible new-item highlighting, and focused Work2 deployment evidence.

Gate:

- `G3-ACTIONABLE-ADVISORY-UI`: each active item exposes its controlled reason, affected project or
  instance, age/freshness, hosted detail link, and safe local investigation route; the UI remains
  authenticated, advisory, read-only, and live through semantic SSE.

Candidate campaign: `implement-actionable-dashboard-attention-and-recent-changes`.

